# Commit Message Format

When drafting or creating a git commit message, always use this structure:

```
TITLE

- bullet item summarizing a change
- another bullet item
```

## Rules

- **TITLE**: Short imperative summary of the overall change (no trailing period). Focus on why/what landed, not a file laundry list.
- **Blank line** between TITLE and bullets.
- Bullets: One concrete change per line. Start with a verb when useful (Add, Fix, Update, Remove). Only add newlines if you are utilizing bullet points; if not using bullet points, avoid adding unnecessary newlines within paragraphs.
- Prefer 2–6 bullets; skip trivial or purely mechanical noise.
- Do not wrap the title in quotes or prefix with `feat:` / `fix:` unless the repo already uses that convention in recent commits.
- Pass the full message via a HEREDOC when running `git commit`.

## Example

```
Add cover letter credit cost estimate API

- Add POST /api/coverLetter/cost that returns cost and discounts without charging
- Expose get_cover_letter_cost MCP tool and document public /api/coverLetter routes
- Add discount labels to creditDiscounts SSOT and use them in RegenerateAction
```